{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1495580-sc-god-incarnations-vs-scions","id":1495580,"title":"[Sc God] Incarnations vs Scions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-10-25T10:09:53-07:00","id":1495580,"title":"[Sc God] Incarnations vs Scions","content":"With Scion God preview manuscript - <b>What is mechanical and setting differences between god's Incarnation vs it's Scions?</b> What's different from Incarnate Scions then? \ud83e\udd14","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-25-2022, 09:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-25T11:43:07-07:00","id":1495587,"title":"","content":"As far as I understand none, except for who controls it. If the player also plays the god it\u2019s a Incarnation, otherwise it\u2019s an Incarnated Scion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-25T17:05:14-07:00","id":1495601,"title":"","content":"I kind of think of it like fruit, odd metaphor I know. If a God is a fruit tree, then an Incarnation is a piece of fruit growing from it. It continues to grow and ripen, and can either be picked or fall off the tree. Either way, once it's separate from the tree, it's not part of the tree anymore, it's its own thing. Incarnated Scions are those separate fruit, either from cutting themselves off (somehow, we're not sure yet, it's going to be in the Companion), or by becoming Demigods, and thus too powerful to remain connected to the God that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-25T18:27:24-07:00","id":1495605,"title":"","content":"Emanuel (the incarnated Scion from Origin, Hero and Demigod) turn back into his original god. So I guess the fruit is not the best metaphor as the fallen fruit turned to grow back to the tree.<br /> <br /> My understand remains, they are the same thing but seen from different points of view.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-26T03:29:13-07:00","id":1495615,"title":"","content":"I think the difference is that an incarnated scion is its own master while a normal incarnation is more of an semi automatic sock-puppet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26520-mugbearer23","name":"Mugbearer23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-26T11:44:30-07:00","id":1495626,"title":"","content":"An incarnation is an automous piece of a god (the god don't control them but can see throught them). They become an incarnate scion if their creator die or if they choose to become a demigod. They can be absorbed by their creator or another god who will remember everything the incarnation experienced.<br /> <br /> An incarnate scion is either the reincarnation of a god who lost all mantles, the reincarnation of a hero with an incomplete mantle, or an ex-incarnation.<br /> <br /> The main difference is the statut of the god they come from: alive = incarnation, dead = incarnate scion.<br /> <br /> The other type of scions are completly free agents and have no link to their god beyond emotional ties.<br /> <br /> The final point are the callings:<br /> -Scions share one calling with their god.<br /> -Incarnation share two callings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26068,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26068-apregis","user":"Apregis","date":". 10-26-2022, 02:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26068-apregis","name":"Apregis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26068_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}